<item><title>Three Republicans urge US Treasury to balance Rwanda sanctions</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/three-republicans-urge-us-treasury-to-balance-rwanda-687fd7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/three-republicans-urge-us-treasury-to-balance-rwanda-687fd7/</guid><category>DR Congo</category><description>Their request follows US sanctions imposed only on Rwanda over its role in destabilising eastern DR Congo.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:30:06 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" length="34755" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>DR Congo&apos;s mining sector gives $1.1 million to Ebola response</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/dr-congo-s-mining-sector-gives-1-1-million-to-ebola-response-be8b16/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/dr-congo-s-mining-sector-gives-1-1-million-to-ebola-response-be8b16/</guid><category>DR Congo</category><description>The money was handed to the coordination body for the country&apos;s 17th Ebola wave, as the World Health Organization said the outbreak remains an international emergency six months.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 06:05:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/dr-congo-s-mining-sector-gives-1-1-million-to-ebola-response-be8b16/share.jpg" length="41776" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/dr-congo-s-mining-sector-gives-1-1-million-to-ebola-response-be8b16/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>UN rights office records 694 violations in DR Congo in September</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/un-rights-office-records-694-violations-in-dr-congo-in-80617d/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/un-rights-office-records-694-violations-in-dr-congo-in-80617d/</guid><category>DR Congo</category><description>The tally rose by more than 41 % from August, with provinces affected by armed conflict accounting for 91 % of documented violations.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 04:38:22 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" length="34755" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kinshasa organisers urge young people to take action for peace</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/kinshasa-organisers-urge-young-people-to-take-action-for-1d630b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/kinshasa-organisers-urge-young-people-to-take-action-for-1d630b/</guid><category>DR Congo</category><description>At a 16 November conference, speakers called on Congolese youth to help prevent conflict and oppose violence against women and girls.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:51:12 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" length="34755" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Kinshasa begins clearing illegal buildings from agricultural land</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/kinshasa-begins-clearing-illegal-buildings-from-550255/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cd/kinshasa-begins-clearing-illegal-buildings-from-550255/</guid><category>DR Congo</category><description>The provincial operation started at Mokali Valley, where farmers say construction had cut the land available for food and vegetable production.</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:06:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" length="34755" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cd.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
